course: dictionary
lesson: 13067
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is the context. «The team had a strong sense of fellowship after winning together.» Here fellowship is a friendly feeling of belonging to a group.
explain: Fellowship can also mean a group of people who share an aim or belief. «The fellowship met every Sunday in the church hall.» The clues are met and church hall, so this is a group, not a feeling. Try each meaning in the sentence and choose the one that fits.
explain: Fellowship can also mean a special paid job for a researcher at a university. «She won a research fellowship to study bees.» The clues research and study tell you it is a job. Matching the clues to the meaning is the key skill.
fact: Fellowship is a noun, and its plural is fellowships.
fact: «Fellowship» means a friendly feeling of sharing and belonging with people who have the same interests.
fact: In church life, «fellowship» means Christians meeting together to share faith, prayer and friendship, often with tea after the service.
fact: «Fellowship» can also mean a group or club of people who share an aim or belief, or a paid job for a researcher at a university.
fact: Phrases you may meet include Christian fellowship, fellowship meal, sense of fellowship and research fellowship.
exercise: «The team had a strong sense of fellowship after winning together.» What does fellowship mean here? | A loud argument | A long, cold walk in the snow | A list of rules for a game | *A friendly feeling of sharing and belonging
exercise: «The fellowship met every Sunday in the church hall.» What does fellowship mean here? | *A group of people who share a belief | A paid job at a university | A kind of sport | A type of tea
exercise: «She won a research fellowship to study bees.» What kind of fellowship is this? | A friendly feeling | *A special paid job for a researcher | A church meal
test: What is a fellowship meal? | *A meal shared by a group of friends who belong together | A meal cooked in a castle | A meal eaten alone at home
test: Which word in «She won a research fellowship at the university» is the best clue that fellowship means a job? | *research | the | she | won
exam: What does fellowship suggest in «The Fellowship of the Ring», a story about a team bound by friendship? | A type of cake | *A team bound by friendship | Bad weather | A quiet library
